   "source": "# A2 — Knowledge-Base Demo\n\nStage 4 (chunk → embed → store — `index/chunk.py`, `index/embed.py`, `index/store.py`) evidence:\nthe demo corpus, the real index pipeline, index statistics, one retrieval example, and one\nretrieval-level worst failure. **OCR quality and the OCR-level worst failure are left as explicit\nplaceholders for Person B in Section 6** — both need a real OCR run against `vision/ocr.py`, which\nisn't index/chunk/embed/store's file to fill in independently.\n\n**Scope note, read before the numbers below:** this notebook runs the pipeline's index stage\nagainst a **small, hand-written demonstration corpus**, not the real 437-page *Rabindra\nRachanabali* Vol. 25 corpus. The real corpus run (`scripts/get_data.sh` → `scripts/build_index.sh`)\nneeds three things that aren't available in this environment yet:\n\n1. **Tesseract-ben installed locally** (`vision/layout.py` and `vision/ocr.py` both call\n   `pytesseract`, which needs the `tesseract` binary + `ben` language data on `PATH` — not present\n   on this machine).\n2. **Two upstream stub fixes**, confirmed by `tests/test_retrieval.py`'s\n   `test_build_knowledge_base_blocked_by_enhance_stub_with_current_config` and\n   `test_build_knowledge_base_blocked_by_pii_stub_once_enhance_disabled`: `ingest/enhance.py` and\n   `governance/pii.py` both still raise `NotImplementedError` on the real\n   `pipeline.build_knowledge_base()` entry point, before Stage 4 is ever reached.\n3. **Real `.ref.txt` / `grading_kit/labels.jsonl` gold labels** — `scripts/get_data.sh` doesn't\n   populate per-page reference transcriptions, and `labels.jsonl` currently holds one placeholder\n   row, so a real OCR pass would (correctly) reject every line at `vision/ocr.py`'s CER gate today.\n\nNone of the three are index/chunk/embed/store's files to fix — see `configs/design_choices.md`'s\nStage 4 row and `reports/pipeline_diagram.md` for the full picture. **Sections 1-5 below are real,\nunmocked code** — the actual `multilingual-e5-base` model and a real FAISS index — only the *input*\ntext is synthetic, standing in for what `vision/ocr.py` would have produced from real scans.\n**Section 6 is Person B's placeholder** and raises on purpose — that's expected, not a bug, and\nSections 1-5 above it will already have run and printed their real results by the time it does."
